== Motion ==

Rendered by the program at 1080p (H.264):

 * [[attachment:plymouth-boot-1080p-h264.mp4|Boot splash]], including a disk passphrase prompt
 * [[attachment:river-growth-1080p-h264.mp4|The river growing]] from its source
 * [[attachment:boot-to-desktop-1080p-h264.mp4|Boot to desktop]]: GRUB, Plymouth, login and desktop (GRUB and login are simulated)

== HDR ==

The light on the water at the fork is brighter than white paper, so the design is a genuine HDR image. It is rendered in scene-linear light, where 1.0 is SDR reference white (203 cd/m², ITU-R BT.2408).

 * '''SDR''' uses a hue-preserving tone curve that leaves everything below the knee untouched.
 * '''HDR''' is the SDR picture plus exactly the light the tone curve removed. The highlights reach about 630 cd/m² (MaxCLL ~631, MaxFALL ~12).

Formats:

 * gain-map AVIF (SDR base plus ISO 21496-1 gain map: one file that looks right on any screen)
 * PQ/BT.2020 AVIF and JPEG XL
 * 16-bit PNG with cICP/mDCv/cLLi
 * scene-linear OpenEXR

== Final ==

 * Desktop wallpaper, dark and light: SVG for 1280x1024, 1600x1200, 1280x800, 1920x1200, 1920x1080, 2560x1080, 1080x2160, 3840x2400, 3840x2160, 5120x2160 (desktop-base layout, with KDE metadata.json and GNOME XML)
 * Light/dark pairing: KDE images/images_dark, GNOME filename-dark
 * Lock screen: the wallpaper images
 * Login screen: background.svg, background-nologo.svg
 * Boot screen: GRUB 2 (grub-16x9.png, grub-4x3.png), Plymouth script theme, installer boot menu splash for isolinux and GRUB (splash.svg, 640x480)
 * Debian Installer: logo_installer.svg and logo_installer_dark.svg (800x75, the same banner for both installer themes), with their PNGs
 * Website banner (800x119) and wiki banner (380x380)
 * High-resolution PNG wallpapers, one native render per screen shape: 3840x2160, 5120x2880, 7680x4320 (16:9); 3840x2400 (16:10); 3000x2000 (3:2); 2560x1664, 3024x1964, 3456x2234 (MacBook); 2732x2048 (4:3); 2560x2048 (5:4); 3440x1440, 3840x1600, 5120x2160 (ultrawide); 5120x1440 (32:9); 1440x3120, 1440x3200, 2160x4320 (phones)
 * HDR masters (see above)

== Source data ==

https://salsa.debian.org/samueloph/distributary and https://github.com/samueloph/distributary (also [[attachment:distributary-src.tar.xz|as a tarball]]): the Python generator; run `make` to rebuild the theme and `make video` for the videos. Build dependencies are all in Debian (python3-numpy, python3-scipy, python3-cairo, python3-gi, gir1.2-rsvg-2.0, python3-pil, python3-contourpy, python3-fonttools, fonts-lato; libavif-bin, libjxl-tools and python3-openimageio for the HDR encodes; ffmpeg for the videos).
